<title>INDIA: World prices push Indian gold, silver higher.</title>
<headline>World prices push Indian gold, silver higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold and silver held modest gains on Tuesday helped by overnight gains in the world market, traders said.</p>
<p>Thin supplies and shortage of ready stock pushed prices higher but demand was sluggish, they said.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 gms) settled 100 rupees higher at 58,800 per piece, after rising 100 rupees on Monday.</p>
<p>The bullion market is closed on Wednesday for Christmas holiday and re-opens on Thursday.</p>
